LRC operation-grid arc-criteria Tournament Analysis (S511)
========================================================================================================
Tie Hamiltonian path: increasing runner label 0->1->... .
Imported S506 criteria keep their native pairwise switch; local criteria
compare runner scalar values induced by pair-cells and operation labels.

Criteria switchboard:
  s506_phase_half                    layer=imported runner gauge   dynamic=True
    observable=pair phase delta frac(x_j-x_i)
    switch=i -> j iff j is clockwise from i by less than 1/2
  s506_lrc_close_sector              layer=imported runner gauge   dynamic=True
    observable=pair phase delta frac(x_j-x_i)
    switch=strict arc only inside the LRC danger sector of width 1/n
  s506_local_moat_min                layer=imported runner gauge   dynamic=True
    observable=vertex score min(left_gap,right_gap)
    switch=larger two-sided local moat points to smaller local moat
  s506_safe_deficit                  layer=imported runner gauge   dynamic=True
    observable=vertex score local deficit below threshold on two adjacent gaps
    switch=smaller deficit points to larger deficit
  s506_threshold_deficit_pressure    layer=imported runner gauge   dynamic=True
    observable=pairwise relief of two-neighbor deficit below 1/n
    switch=blocker points to runner whose threshold deficit it removes more
  origin_clearance_rank              layer=runner geometry         dynamic=True
    observable=runner distance from observer 0
    switch=farther from 0 points to closer to 0
  local_two_guard                    layer=runner geometry         dynamic=True
    observable=min(left adjacent gap, right adjacent gap)
    switch=larger two-sided guard points to smaller guard
  incident_danger_sum                layer=pair-cell aggregate     dynamic=True
    observable=sum_j max(0,1/N-dist(i,j,t))
    switch=more incident threshold danger points to less danger
  incident_close_count               layer=pair-cell aggregate     dynamic=True
    observable=number of incident pair-cells below the LRC threshold
    switch=more close incident pair-cells points to fewer
  dyadic_branch_pressure             layer=operation grid          dynamic=False
    observable=sum_j v2(|v_i-v_j|)
    switch=higher x*2 branch pressure points to lower
  odd_core_branch_count              layer=operation grid          dynamic=False
    observable=number of distinct odd cores among incident speed gaps
    switch=more x+2 branch diversity points to less
  same_odd_chain_degree              layer=operation grid          dynamic=False
    observable=count of runners sharing the same odd-core doubling chain
    switch=more same-chain incidence points to less
  additive_shadow_degree             layer=operation grid          dynamic=False
    observable=participation in speed equations a+b=c or |a-b|=c
    switch=more additive-shadow incidence points to less
  multiplicative_shadow_degree       layer=operation grid          dynamic=False
    observable=divisibility incidence among nonzero speeds
    switch=more multiplicative-shadow incidence points to less
  product_sum_interface              layer=operation grid          dynamic=False
    observable=sum_j 1/(1+|(v_i mod N)(v_j mod N)-(N-1)|)
    switch=closer to product-sum interface points to farther
  dyadic_danger_curvature            layer=hybrid                  dynamic=True
    observable=incident danger deficit weighted by 1+v2(|v_i-v_j|)
    switch=more deep-branch danger points to less
  odd_chain_danger                   layer=hybrid                  dynamic=True
    observable=incident danger deficit restricted to same odd-core chains
    switch=more same-chain danger points to less
  additive_danger_interface          layer=hybrid                  dynamic=True
    observable=incident danger deficit weighted by additive-shadow pair incidence
    switch=more additive danger points to less
  multiplicative_danger_interface    layer=hybrid                  dynamic=True
    observable=incident danger deficit weighted by divisibility pair incidence
    switch=more multiplicative danger points to less
  product_sum_danger                 layer=hybrid                  dynamic=True
    observable=incident danger deficit weighted by product-sum closeness
    switch=more product-sum danger points to less

