A000568, x+2/x*2, AND OPERATION INTERFACES
========================================================================================================
A000568 terms from the odd-partition Burnside formula:
  1, 1, 2, 4, 12, 56, 456, 6880, 191536, 9733056
Only odd cycle partitions contribute; this is the quotient-level analogue
of an odd-core survival rule for complete orientations.

2-adic operation grid up to 48:
  horizontal move: odd core x -> x+2
  vertical move:   branch height x -> 2x
  odd core  1: 1 -> 2 -> 4 -> 8 -> 16 -> 32
  odd core  3: 3 -> 6 -> 12 -> 24 -> 48
  odd core  5: 5 -> 10 -> 20 -> 40
  odd core  7: 7 -> 14 -> 28
  odd core  9: 9 -> 18 -> 36
  odd core 11: 11 -> 22 -> 44
  odd core 13: 13 -> 26
  odd core 15: 15 -> 30
  odd core 17: 17 -> 34
  odd core 19: 19 -> 38
  odd core 21: 21 -> 42
  odd core 23: 23 -> 46

How the script turns operations into arc criteria:
  addition: speed equations a+b=c or |a-b|=c give additive-shadow degree.
  multiplication: divisibility and doubling branches give x*2 pressure.
  product-sum: (a-1)(b-1)=N-1 gives a critical interface score.
  hybrid: multiply each static operation label by current 1/N danger.

Two-factor product-sum landmarks:
  N=14: two-factor (2,14)->28; seed 1^11 + 2 2 5
  N=18: two-factor (2,18)->36; seed 1^15 + 2 3 4
  N=21: two-factor (2,21)->42, (3,11)->33, (5,6)->30; seed 1^18 + 3 3 3
  N=24: two-factor (2,24)->48; seed 1^22 + 2 24
  N=30: two-factor (2,30)->60; seed 1^26 + 2 2 3 3

